speechtext:
The weights under these grade standards are not put according to the weights in the section to which my hon. friend has referred: The section says:
08. In contracts for the sale and delivery of any of the undermentioned articles, the bushel shall be determined by weighing, unless a bushel by measure is specially agreed upon and the weight equivalent to a' bushel shall, except as hereinafter provided, be'as follows:_
Barley, forty-eight pounds;
Buckwheat, forty-eight pounds;
Flax-seed, fifty-six pounds;
Indian corn, fifty-six pounds;
Oats, thirty-four pounds;
Peas, sixty pounds;
Rye, fifty-six pounds;
Wheat, sixty pounds.
